# Bun loads this for `bun test` run from the repository root, as `npm test` and CI do, before anything starts, so
# every process the tests spawn inherits it.
#
# TEMPORARY, and bad: remove GOMAXPROCS=1 once TypeScript ships a tsc built with a Go release that fixes
# https://github.com/golang/go/issues/81759 (the fix is https://go.dev/cl/840845), and upgrade typescript to it.
# It makes every TypeScript and graph process the tests start single-threaded, so the TypeScript parts of the suite
# run several times slower, and the tests no longer exercise the parallelism users get.
#
# It's needed for now because Go 1.26 and 1.27 can deadlock a process that's collecting garbage while its other
# threads sit in a blocking read on a pipe, which is how `tsc --api` waits for requests. The stuck tsc never answers,
# so a test waits until it times out, in about one full run in ten. Only GOMAXPROCS=1 avoids it: GOMAXPROCS=2 and
# GODEBUG=asyncpreemptoff=1 don't. Only tests get this setting; sightread and shorthand run as before.
GOMAXPROCS=1
